{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.ClassicalTraceFloor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ClassicalTraceFloor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.classicalTraceFloor_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.classicalTraceFloor_lt","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ClassicalTraceFloor.lean#L149-L153","doc":"And it is strictly below `2^{−A}`, so it decays at least geometrically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.classicalTraceFloor_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.classicalTraceFloor_pos","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ClassicalTraceFloor.lean#L137-L147","doc":"The floor is strictly positive for `A ≥ 2`.\n\n`A ≥ 2`, not `A ≥ 1`: at `A = 1` the two exponents coincide (`1 − 2 = −1`) and\nthe floor is exactly `0`. Every nucleus has `A ≥ 2`, so the bound covers the\nwhole range of interest, but the boundary case is real and is why the hypothesis\nis not `1 ≤ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.classical_floor_of_cycle_counts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.classical_floor_of_cycle_counts","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ClassicalTraceFloor.lean#L103-L122","doc":"**The floor, end to end.**\n\n`hfree` and `hmerge` are step 2 (the cycle counts, computed from the braid\nwords); `hSWfree` and `hSWatom` are step 1 (Schur–Weyl at `q = 1`, a published\ntheorem Mathlib does not carry). Everything between them is derived.\n\nThe conclusion is exactly the form the probes measured — `1/8` at `A = 2`,\n`7/128` at `A = 4` — but here it is not extrapolated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.classicalTraceFloor_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.classicalTraceFloor_chain","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ClassicalTraceFloor.lean#L95-L101","doc":"**The closed form, from the chain cycle counts.** Pure exponent bookkeeping:\n`2A − 3A = −A` and `(A+1) − 3A = 1 − 2A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.cAtom_eq_of_free_and_merges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.cAtom_eq_of_free_and_merges","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ClassicalTraceFloor.lean#L84-L93","doc":"**The atom-word cycle count follows from the free count and the merges.**\n\n`c_free = 2A` (two cycles per free nucleon) together with \"each of the `A−1`\ninterfaces merges one pair\" forces `c_atom = A + 1`. Stated separately because\nit is the step where the chain adjacency enters, and it is pure arithmetic once\nthe merge count is granted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.classicalTraceFloor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.classicalTraceFloor","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ClassicalTraceFloor.lean#L76-L82","doc":"The classical (`q = 1`) trace difference, as it comes out of the two cycle\ncounts: `2^{c_free − n} − 2^{c_atom − n}`.\n\nInteger exponents throughout — `c_atom − n` is negative in every case of\ninterest, so `zpow` is the honest type. ","signatureChunk":0}]}